","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5491749?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShadowManu","html_url":"https://github.com/ShadowManu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShadowManu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShadowManu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShadowManu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShadowManu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShadowManu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShadowManu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShadowManu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShadowManu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShadowManu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-02-04T20:03:10Z","updated_at":"2018-02-04T20:03:10Z","body":"@chanlito for learning purposes, how would you create that decorator: What it decorates, how it works and why it works? Haven't really authored decorators myself.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/362934969/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/362959774","html_url":"https://github.com/nestjs/nest/pull/383#issuecomment-362959774","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/383","id":362959774,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2Mjk1OTc3NA==","user":{"login":"chanlito","id":15667259,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjY3MjU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15667259?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanlito","html_url":"https://github.com/chanlito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanlito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanlito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanlito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanlito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanlito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanlito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanlito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanlito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanlito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-02-05T01:39:55Z","updated_at":"2018-02-05T01:39:55Z","body":"@ShadowManu I was thinking of something like the following without using the constructor:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\n@Dto() // or @Dto({ transform: true, strip: true, reject: false })\r\nexport class CreateCatsDto {\r\n  @IsNotEmpty()\r\n  @IsString()\r\n  readonly name: string;\r\n\r\n  // @Transform() or @Type()\r\n  readonly color: string;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow we can strip unwanted incoming fields, validate and tranform.\r\n\r\nWith reflect metadata we can achieve the `@Dto()` above.\r\n\r\nThen somewhere in our nest bootstrap, we can do the following.\r\n\r\n```ts\r\n...\r\napp.useGlobalPipe(new ValidationPipe(this.reflector))\r\n...\r\n```\r\n\r\nInside the validation pipe we could check if the class has been decorated by `@Dto`, if it has we run transformation or validation on it, else just return the value. 😉","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/362959774/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/comments/363022315","html_url":"https://github.com/nestjs/nest/pull/383#issuecomment-363022315","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/